a":80,"verse":9,"english":"Thus accosted by us, the magnanimous Laks maņa with his gaze ever fixed on virtue, humbly observed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c21047ddff940dab500331edf0497b014bfb592b726bfc834201707156ecfb94","compact":"5bfc35887b9808f0562dd3c28d37db96b597fe7a297a18785aa84dde96c028ed","nasal":"5bfc35887b9808f0562dd3c28d37db96b597fe7a297a18785aa84dde96c028ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":10,"english":"How, Dasaratha's son sleeping on the earth with Sītā, can I attain sleep, or life, or happiness?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.685,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"800694227fa52820bd74e27ab858bd5ad5903f6e5e25333977d6bdd5d5d0c093","compact":"6cb86ccbffdc5fc1a466adebfa6a869147ca837f72f37e55876b5a746826e322","nasal":"6cb86ccbffdc5fc1a466adebfa6a869147ca837f72f37e55876b5a746826e322"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":11,"english":"How see him who is capable of bearing in battle the onslaught of the gods and the Asuras combined, sleeping in a cave on grass?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2f644f893b8798c4500edc2e966a9631df6369bfa89eed0069cbcbd4207b7cdd","compact":"bac878c79f98df391b07481fb07e966c82297dc0c1a5f868ab84b8c3496e9e0c","nasal":"bac878c79f98df391b07481fb07e966c82297dc0c1a5f868ab84b8c3496e9e0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":12,"english":"It is by virtue of mighty austerities and uncommon exertions that Dasaratha has obtained this son of his crowned with every auspicious sign. He being banished, the king shall not live long; and the Earth shall certainly be widowed soon.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b8d8ebbab3316d8507d38ee2c491691b203c9ba097b1c0b0a859aa4aa81e9a2","compact":"d30b0c8a2a14fc38323f6d83be89394d5651826fdcf38f57c33c3c63e441a5a1","nasal":"d30b0c8a2a14fc38323f6d83be89394d5651826fdcf38f57c33c3c63e441a5a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":13,"english":"It is by virtue of mighty austerities and uncommon exertions that Dasaratha has obtained this son of his crowned with every auspicious sign. He being banished, the king shall not live long; and the Earth shall certainly be widowed soon.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"440201b5a2b4dc0b69a177cd525a0ac6ecdaaf590cead9a41f048b7565db5e58","compact":"0642d260c34747db070478092d53b35ff6c2bcd9562e978d3924a1001da98020","nasal":"0642d260c34747db070478092d53b35ff6c2bcd9562e978d3924a1001da98020"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":14,"english":"Having bewailed aloud, by this time have the women got exhausted; and surely the king's mansion is to-day still.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a618a38b6ea3599c58778a4fa3315a3ae5765f6ae296a0abe4dbf1b76aea0779","compact":"900f782cbdfb09545d7c75eaf324602d2d90673bdd4de75e05d9e0bd7cc72927","nasal":"900f782cbdfb09545d7c75eaf324602d2d90673bdd4de75e05d9e0bd7cc72927"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":15,"english":"I do not expect that either Kausalyā or the king or my mother is alive. If they live, it can be for this night only.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad26fbf89515520e765dcef871f2e73d4af7521983e5bd5f456a17fc68eb7f05","compact":"da1cca1b067d2988003740eb321fbf9de743198422bb993dedb13b32988981ab","nasal":"da1cca1b067d2988003740eb321fbf9de743198422bb993dedb13b32988981ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":16,"english":"Even if my mother live seeing Satrughna, that mother of a hero, the afflicted Kausalyā, will (surely) resign her existence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e63ec87303d9c8b8ff94597b9cfd8740944fa793e6df5215aaca5b20a6298d9","compact":"40d324d66341e180c90d0bf7cddce064e2e9c3cb60c435cbfaa8d9e320a900d3","nasal":"40d324d66341e180c90d0bf7cddce064e2e9c3cb60c435cbfaa8d9e320a900d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":17,"english":"Saying, All is lost, All is lost, with his desire unattained, my father having failed to install Rāma in the kingdom, will resign his existence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"72ab5ad8f908bd9f40f5aa9a11cbb62cd4f76de2b4e4bfacbbd0b98dff50cfd0","compact":"8abd60d9aaac10927a1543c6e86815b64865e6920aaf1a0a4925e2899c25b6f7","nasal":"8a4ff701aaddb4505b0ff7cd0cfe6894b8db626fee2d601137743d018bd72270"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":18,"english":"Blessed are they that when the time shall come for the same, shall perform the funeral ceremonies of the king, my deceased sire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.872,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad6344d61e821565115cd7066d7373aa9930db148d6ebd838e5ff88ba0214aaf","compact":"b7247c6f666826b6ba6886fd7acb2fddadc738339998fbd8d287eab5ef64aec2","nasal":"415ff5ccf527b0a4eb808b40ca3acca84d4f27a1c843f98dceb36cef5bd7a195"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-80-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":80,"verse":19,"english":"Then shall they with happy hearts range the looking terraces, with the highways laid out orderly, crowned with lordly edifices, adorned with various gems, crowded by cars and elephants and horses, resounding with the notes of trumpets, abounding in auspicious things, filled with fat and contented people, having gardens and pleasure-houses, and possessed of divers classed of men indulging festal mirth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-86-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2080019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5a4df8d2911ea8f19ae24b934d118b16f577adbce6373cbffe55e72cd20420e","compact":"bdecd82ddfe2939361ae6f0390cc140d92dc6b9173d40dbf58798daa1f8a5aa7","nasal":"b7